maria_cs: Customer reported a 422 from /v1/rerank when they pass a per-document `query` field. Payload and error pasted below, can someone confirm expected shape?

maria_cs: Payload we received (redacted IDs):
```json
{
  "query": { "text": "find best match for phrase" },
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "doc-1",
      "metadata": { "source": "kb" },
      "query": { "text": "override term" },
      "passages": [ { "text": "..." } ]
    },
    {
      "id": "doc-2",
      "passages": [ { "text": "..." } ]
    }
  ]
}
```

maria_cs: Error: `422 Unprocessable Entity - ambiguous query field found in documents` plus a chunk of stacktrace from rerank-service. Customer insists they always put per-doc query to allow doc-scoped reranking.

sam_engineer: short answer: our rerank contract treats `query` as a reserved root-level key. If a doc contains a `query` key we currently treat it as candidate data and try to map it to candidate schema which collides with the root `query`. That ambiguity triggers the 422 when both exist.

reid_dev: adding detail: the service expects either:
- root-level `query` with `documents` or `candidates` (documents are containers, candidates are explicit items)
- OR per-candidate `text`/`content` fields (e.g., in `candidates`) but not a nested `query` object inside each document.

reid_dev: Example accepted shapes:
```json
{
  "query": { "text": "find best match" },
  "documents": [ { "id": "doc-1", "passages": [ { "text": "..." } ] } ]
}
```

and for candidate-style:
```json
{
  "query": { "text": "..." },
  "candidates": [ { "id": "c1", "text": "..." } ]
}
```

lucy_support: customer use-case: they want ranking per-document where each doc has its own local query + scoring options. They thought putting `query` inside doc would be the most expressive. Is there a way to support that without breaking the service?

sam_engineer: currently no — the API uses `query` as the discriminant. Two paths: we can (1) flatten their payload before sending to rerank (our support proxy does that for them), e.g., move per-doc query into `metadata.query_text` and call rerank per-doc sequentially (expensive), or (2) extend API to accept `documents[].local_query` (non-breaking) and have server merge appropriately (engineering change).

oliver_infra: FYI there was also a recent deploy that tightened schema validation to reject unknown `query` objects nested under `documents`. That made the 422s more explicit. Before it was silently ignoring nested keys which led to wrong scores.

alice_pm: what's the risk/effort to add `documents[].local_query` as first-class? We should estimate because customers are hitting this pattern.

reid_dev: quick estimate: ~2-3 sprint-days to add server-side merge + tests + docs, plus a migration plan. Short-term: we can provide a support shim in the SDK and our support team can take the messy payload and transform it to an accepted shape.

maria_cs: can you paste the minimal repro transform we used to validate? I'll give that to the customer as a workaround.

sam_engineer: minimal transform (JS pseudo):
```js
// flatten per-doc query into candidate-compatible call
const transformedCandidates = [];
for (const d of payload.documents) {
  const q = d.query ? d.query.text : payload.query.text;
  for (const p of (d.passages || [])) {
    transformedCandidates.push({ id: d.id + '::' + (p.id || 'p0'), text: p.text, doc_query: q });
  }
}
// call rerank with root query = payload.query (or placeholder) and candidates = transformedCandidates
```

lucy_support: customer accepts workaround if we provide clear instructions + sample cURL.

maria_cs: I'll send the snippet and offer to run the transform for them in support if needed. Can we also open an internal ticket to track a proper API change?

sam_engineer: opening issue: https://redwood.example.com/issue/RI-4721 created. Tagging @alice_pm for prioritization. :white_check_mark:

rerank_bot: CI note: schema-validator job failed on latest master when nested `query` detected, see logs at CI#9876.

maria_cs: thanks all — I'll follow up with customer and paste the transformed payload. If they still see weird scores after flattening, I'll escalate to @reid_dev with the raw payload and request a deep-dive. :pray:
